## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates a practical monocular solution for tool manipulation that must handle new categories, operate under strict latency constraints, and support few-shot on-device adaptation in cluttered workshop environments.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 6-DoF pose estimation from 2D-3D correspondences
- Few-shot on-device adaptation using adapter modules
- Synthetic and real data strategy with domain randomization
- Real-time performance requirements and edge GPU optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
// PnP pose estimation sketch
function estimatePose2D3D(keypoints2D, model3D, camera) {
  // use perspective-n-point algorithm
  return cv.solvePnP(model3D, keypoints2D, camera.matrix, camera.distortion);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design joint monocular depth and motion estimation under dynamic scenes and adverse weather, optimized for edge devices and quick adaptation to new conditions.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth and scene-flow fusion in cluttered traffic
- Temporal fusion across frames for stability
- On-device 5-shot adaptation with lightweight adapters

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-architecture sketch
function forward(x) {
  const z = encoder(x); // shared features
  const d = depthHead(z);
  const s = flowHead(z);
  const o = objMotionHead(z);
  const t = temporalFuse([d, s, o]);
  return {depth: d, sceneFlow: s, objectMotion: o, fused: t};
}
```

